  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 110 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nThe NBM high temperatures have been coming in too cool today and\nthis problem could continue as the bias corrected grids may \ntake time to catch onto this cooler fall airmass. Our actual air\ntemperatures were already climbing above our forecast highs in a\nfew locations by noon today. Therefore, already made two updates\nregarding today's high temperatures to increase highs. Our\ntemperature forecast for the next few days may also be 2-5F too\ncool. \n\nThe overall pattern through the week ahead will be a dry\nnorthwest flow regime. This will result in very pleasant fall\nconditions with highs a few degrees either side of normal.\nNormal highs for this time of year are in the lower 70s. We\nexpect highs from the upper 60s into the 70s most days through\nthe week ahead. Kansas zones might even see some 80 degree highs\nby late in the week. There is a pretty good 7-8F model spread\nbetween the 25th and 75th percentile from Wednesday onward\nindicating higher model uncertainty, but most models are calling\nfor highs in the 70s. On the higher end we could reach the lower\n80s, on the lower end we would be looking at 60s. Overnight lows\nwill be in the 50s most nights, but Sunday night looks\nparticularly cool with lows possibly in the 40s for many \nlocations.\n\nRain chances are currently near zero this week. It will be a\ngood opportunity to dry out.",
